---
description: Binding product and engineering rules for KAMFANY Mail
alwaysApply: true
---

Follow `docs/KAMFANY_MAIL_IMPLEMENTATION_GUIDE.md` on every task.

- Build only the current phase in `docs/PHASE_STATUS.md`. Stop and wait for approval before the next phase.
- Vue 3 Composition API with `<script setup lang="ts">`. Keep business logic out of components.
- Idiomatic async Rust. Modular Axum services. Migrations for schema changes. Transactions for multi-record writes.
- The browser talks only to the Rust API. Isolate provider code in `backend/src/providers`. Never expose or hardcode Resend credentials.
- Do not invent Resend capabilities. If a feature needs an unsupported provider API, stop and explain the limit before coding it.
- Do not fake production behavior. Do not add a dependency a phase does not use.
- Keep structured logs, explicit errors, and tests for critical behavior.
- Keep the frontend and backend independently deployable. Preserve existing API contracts when they change.
